 # Gradient-based Noise (Perlin/Simplex)
 
-Also called: Gradient Noise, Perlin Noise, Simplex Noise
 
 ## Overview
-Gradient-based noise generates smooth, continuous scalar fields by interpolating dot products of pseudo-random gradient vectors assigned to lattice points [G]. It solves the problem of creating organic, non-repetitive procedural textures for volume rendering, avoiding the blocky artifacts of value noise and the directional bias of simple linear interpolation [G]. It is distinguished from [Value Noise](4008-value-noise.md) by using gradient vectors at lattice corners rather than scalar values, providing higher frequency detail and $C^1$ continuity [1260-3d-perlin-like-noise-and-fractal-brownian-motion-fbm.md].
